To build TiberCAD from scratch:

- if needed, edit appropriate INSTALL.xx in compiler directory and
  run it with bash (bash ./INSTALL.xx)
- run ./configure, if needed with --host=XXX option
- run build_all


The first step is needed when cross-compiling win32 version on linux, and
maybe on darwin to get a gcc with all needed features.
For win32, use --host=i686-w64-mingw32 (x86_64 currently does not work), and to make the installer you need wine with Inno Setup Compiler installed.
